# Coordination — Blocking Queues & Actors (LLD Revision Guide)

A crisp revision guide for coordination problems in concurrent systems. Covers wait/notify, bounded blocking queues, graceful shutdown, the actor model, and real-world producer-consumer patterns.

> **Core idea:** Concurrency correctness is about *who touches what, when*. Coordination is about *how independent threads hand work to each other safely*.

