## 11. Common Mistakes to Avoid

| Mistake | Consequence | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| **Unbounded queue** | OOM under load | Always pass a capacity |
| **`wait()` without predicate** | Spurious wakeups break logic | `wait(lock, [&]{ return cond; })` |
| **Modifying state without holding mutex** | Race conditions | Lock before every read/write of shared state |
| **Running task inside the lock** | Serializes all work | Release lock before invoking the task |
| **Swallowing shutdown signal** | Threads can't be stopped | Always check shutdown flag in wait predicate |
| **Sharing data between actors directly** | Defeats the entire model | Communicate only via `send()` |
| **Using `notify_one()` for shutdown** | Only wakes one waiter | Use `notify_all()` to broadcast |
| **Infinite worker loop with no exit** | Hangs on shutdown | Check `running_` flag in predicate |
| **Sizing queue too large** | Memory bloat, stale work | Size ~ throughput × burst seconds |
| **Sizing queue too small** | Producers blocked frequently | Increase based on real burst patterns |

